[36m(TaskRunner pid=180524)[0m For \(n\) to be odd, \(a = 0\). Thus, \(n = 3^b \times 5^c \times 7^d\). We need \(n \equiv 1 \mod 5\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=180524)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=180524)[0m - For \(c = 0\), \(n = 3^b \times 7^d\). We need \(3^b \times 7^d \equiv 1 \mod 5\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=180524)[0m   - When \(d = 0\), \(n = 3^b \equiv 1 \mod 5\) ⇒ \(b = 0\) or \(b = 4\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=180524)[0m   - When \(d = 1\), \(n = 3^b \times 7 \equiv 3^b \times 2 \equiv 1 \mod 5\) ⇒ \(3^b \equiv 3 \mod 5\) ⇒ \(b = 1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=180524)[0m 
